WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:09.820
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:20.480
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.910
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.570
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:07.050
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:14.350
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:21.050
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:28.280
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.160
The technology
in my country, Shoukoku…

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.030
…is the most
cutting edge in Daikuuriku.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:31.730
Even so, we still can’t build a plane
that can fly above the clouds…

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:37.090
…and if lightning struck the gas tank,
it would instantly explode into flames.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.050
We’re aware of
this danger but must go forth.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.800
Beyond the waves’ crests…

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.700
Kyuukoku.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:10.400
This sublime and peaceful
country carries a certain secret.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:16.840
To gain this secret, my country
has mounted countless invasions.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.660
But we have always been thwarted.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.960
Kyuukoku’s secret.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.240
The demonic Simoun.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:44.320
No other vessel in Daikuuriku
is capable of flying so freely…

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.330
…throughout the skies.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:50.290
<b>Fallen Wings</b>

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.680
It’s a routine patrol flight.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.660
The governors are observing today,
so they’re making a show of it.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.550
Neviril-sama…

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.700
Neviril-sama…
Call her “Sibylla Aurea.”

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.280
She glitters like gold…

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.020
Was your father well, Neviril?

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.990
Amuria, you’re tormenting me.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.370
There are hundreds
of Ri Majon patterns…

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.410
…and depending on the mix,
they take infinite shapes.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:59.670
We’ve forgotten what many
of those patterns signify…

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:04.390
…but the Simoun sibyllae are
always prepared to rediscover them.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:09.120
Your daughter is
an outstanding pilot, as expected.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.390
It seems she’s become a
full-fledged pilot, which relieves me.

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:18.290
Indeed, she’s become the premier
Simoun sibylla called “Sibylla Aurea.”

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.360
Her prayers may
indeed be exceptional…

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:25.970
…but if she’s used in war,
we’re only tarnishing an old tradition.

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:27.200
High Priestess…

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:31.410
How can we use prayers meant
only for the gods for war?

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:36.740
By deploying Simouns to the border,
we display Tempus Spatium’s power…

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:41.720
…and can repulse these nefarious
invaders in a peaceful manner.

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:45.880
Is that not
in accordance with God’s will?

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:02.270
My father made a point of ordering
Chor Tempest to mobilize…

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.360
…since he wanted to look
good for the spectators.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.360
It’s because Chor Tempest
is the best chor.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:13.250
Amuria, it’s not becoming of
a sibylla to use the word “best.”

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.320
You’re wrong.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:19.320
We’re only offering up our prayers.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:23.330
By achieving a perfect Ri Majon,
we give comfort to Tempus Spatium.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.330
It is our duty to become powerful.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.260
More and more powerful.

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:34.010
Powerful? For what purpose?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:44.230
Neviril!
Do you hear what I’m hearing?

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:53.030
This is…

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:23.530
This is Neviril of Chor Tempest.
Are you all right?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.540
They fell… Which Simoun fell?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.580
All of them.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.360
Chor Caput has fallen.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.530
We are the only survivors.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:43.270
Send a messenger
to Guragief-sama right away.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:47.920
Sibylla Aurea, please be careful.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.730
That’s impossible.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:13.730
A Simoun was shot down…

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:15.780
Calm down, Neviril.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:19.490
We knew this day
would come someday.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:23.450
Ever since the day they decided
to send us into battle with Simouns.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.780
No, Amuria.
Simouns are divine aircraft.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.720
No matter what country
develops a flying machine…

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.430
…they cannot match the craft of gods.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:38.850
That’s why enemies flee
at the sight of a Simoun…

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:40.430
They flee when they see us…

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.100
My lady…

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.310
Did I say something?

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.300
Are we going to die?

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:51.400
But I’m with you,
Para-sama, I don’t mind dying.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.990
I still have things to do. I can’t die.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.560
You mean Neviril?

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.280
Did I allow such familiar
addressing, Kaim?

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.040
Oh, we need your permission.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:08.750
I wonder if they’re good? Shoukoku’s
flying machines float like clouds, right?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.820
There must be some mistake.

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:14.290
There’s no question.
Simouns can’t fall.

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:17.930
We just fly them,
and the enemy runs off.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.720
Sublime harmony…

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.340
Neviril, let’s try the Emerald Ri Majon.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:28.410
That again. We don’t have the ancient
Ri Majon patterns fully analyzed yet.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:32.850
Simoun sibyllae of legend succeeded
with an Emerald Ri Majon…

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.730
…and served as priestesses
close to Tempus Spatium.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.900
If we succeed,
we can end up that way too.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:43.360
You’re so impatient. Now isn’t
the time to think of such things.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.160
I want to become more powerful.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:50.870
That’s the border. I’m taking us down.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:18.090
The Simouns are divine aircraft.

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:22.960
True, the technology is on
a whole different level than ours.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:29.000
But if we can discover their secret,
our country will make great advances.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:49.980
The Falcon Ri Majon.

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:13.830
If they dare to enter our country,
then they’ll never leave.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.760
They’re just flying after all.
They’re not like Simouns.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:26.140
A Simoun inscribes patterns upon
the sky using the light from its wake.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:29.500
That is a Ri Majon.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:33.850
We haven’t yet discovered
why it’s so powerful.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:41.010
Once we find out this secret,
our nation’s technology will advance.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:46.820
But Kyuukoku has long kept
the secrets of the Simouns from us.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.550
We’ve been taught that Simouns
send those who pursue them to hell.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:57.520
But now I see.
The Simouns are mere machines.

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.000
There’s no hell in sight.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:08.050
How can there be so many?

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:12.770
The Simouns aren’t divine aircraft.
They’re just machines.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.520
So they can fall.
It’s possible to shoot them down.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:20.150
Someday we’ll solve
the Ri Majon mystery.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:25.530
The era of Kyuukoku’s monopoly
on Simoun technology will end.

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:29.690
There are a lot, but they’re slowpokes!
Shoot them all down!

00:13:29.690 --> 00:13:31.200
Shark Ri Majon!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.630
Six-unit Iron Ri Majon…

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:46.840
Got it!

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:02.150
They’ll erase the glyph!

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:03.860
What’s with them?

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:08.710
If they fail to draw a glyph,
they can’t achieve a Ri Majon.

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:23.880
The Emerald Ri Majon, Neviril.
A miracle is sure to happen.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:26.920
No, Amuria.
There’s no telling what will happen…

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:31.140
I want to become stronger.
I want to become stronger, Neviril.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:35.890
I can’t go on like this!
So many things getting in our way.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.260
They’re taking our wings away.

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:40.650
That’s right… We’ve got to fight.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:45.780
Amuria!

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:49.780
I said I want to become stronger.
You understand, right, Neviril?

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.120
We can do it.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:11.720
Let’s go. To where we can be free.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.550
Neviril, more… More powerful, Neviril.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:56.040
Yes.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.400
She was so beautiful…

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:10.360
Neviril, don’t look! You can’t
kill them if you see their eyes!

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.530
Neviril!

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:21.450
The Emerald Ri Majon failed.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:23.960
What’s going on?

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:40.890
Neviril!

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:44.600
Tempus Spatium is full of fury.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.400
The Simouns are machines.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:49.820
Not divine aircraft at all.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:54.740
My country will surely
discover this demonic secret…

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:58.280
But could it be…

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:01.160
…they really were…

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.170
Huh?

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:21.740
Sibylla Aurea is exhausted.
I’ll relay your message.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.200
Paraietta-sama.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.620
Um, we’re…

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.700
…leaving the ship?

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.040
Yes.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:37.030
We intend to go to
the Spring to meet with Onasia.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.010
If you go, you can’t be a sibylla.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:42.970
You’ll never be able to touch
a Simoun again. You’re sure?

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.140
Yes.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.470
I intend to become a male.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:50.200
To become just as gallant as you.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:53.940
It’s unseemly to speak of
such intentions to others. Go on.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:09.290
Do you plan to stare at
her door forever, senpai?

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:14.250
I am unable
to assuage a sibylla’s grief.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:18.210
All I can do is grieve just as much.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:33.300
Are you a trainee?

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.020
This is the sanctuary
of the sibyllae. Leave.

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:42.390
Are the priestesses
in better humor now?

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:46.260
Should the moon be covered
by clouds, the stars fade too.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.410
That’s where they stand.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:52.920
They have lost a precious pair.
They’re not to blame.

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:59.780
Chor Tempest has lost three sibyllae.
Not counting those going to the Spring.

00:19:59.780 --> 00:20:02.750
Meaning it is no longer our elite chor?

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:03.840
Dux.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.110
What is it?

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:08.190
Sibylla Floe. Sibylla Rimone.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:09.980
Actually, this child…

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:11.840
Sibylla? But…

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:16.060
She’s young, but we’re having her join
Chor Tempest as a special case.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:25.770
This is most irregular. Promoting
such a young trainee to sibylla.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:30.570
But if we don’t, we’ll no longer
be able to protect the Simouns.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:33.790
So is that doll your only replacement?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.940
No, there’s one more before launch.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.340
Another oddball?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:40.770
Another oddball?
No, a normal one, Captain.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:52.390
Who’s that?

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:58.020
Wow! This is a Simoun, huh?

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:00.980
I’ve never seen the real thing before.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.700
Sibylla Aer?
I expected you to arrive sooner.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:17.980
Shoukoku’s planes are advancing
along the border once again.

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.630
I’m sending Chor Tempest.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:22.460
Isn’t that futile?

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.220
I’m sure Neviril won’t like it.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:26.630
I agree.

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:31.310
I don’t see Neviril and Paraietta here.

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:33.810
They won’t want to fly.

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:35.390
I’m so scared…

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:39.600
We have nothing but
the Simouns to fight with.

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:43.840
But is it God’s will that
we do something like this?

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:45.360
I’m going up.

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:48.030
I’m on my way.

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:50.410
Please wait, Sibylla Aer!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.950
She’s probably not a priestess.

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:14.740
That’s a Simile training craft!

00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:17.020
That can’t achieve a Ri Majon…

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:30.160
The rest of you can go on praying.

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:33.810
I’ve come here to go into battle.

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:48.010
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:52.240
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:59.280
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:07.150
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:19.770
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.770 --> 00:23:24.980
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:28.950
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.950 --> 00:23:32.890
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:38.810
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:44.370
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:47.800
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:53.470
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:59.870
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:12.470
Simouns can’t
possibly fall, and yet they have.

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:17.620
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>The Blue Spring</b>

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:20.020
The Blue Spring.
